<title>USA: U.S. Office Products buys 30 new companies.</title>
<headline>U.S. Office Products buys 30 new companies.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON, D.C. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Office Products said on Thursday that it has agreed to buy 30 new companies with about $605 million in annual revenues for about $208 million in stock and $61 million in cash.</p>
<p>The company said the acquisitions will be &quot;highly accretive&quot; to future earnings per share and increase its annualized revenue run rate to $2.9 billion.</p>
<p>Together the companies have about $605 million in annual revenues, U.S. Office said.</p>
